{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387220-which-of-the-orisha-corresponds-to-baron-samedi","id":1387220,"title":"Which of the Orisha corresponds to Baron Samedi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-10T03:23:14-07:00","id":1387220,"title":"Which of the Orisha corresponds to Baron Samedi?","content":"One of the other guys in my RPG group is talking about running Scion. One idea I have for a character is a scion of Baron Samedi, the loa of the dead; but none of the Orisha list Baron Samedi as an alias. The books I have are Scion 2e Origin and Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:32:45-07:00","id":1387221,"title":"","content":"Samedi doesn't really correlate with any of the Orisha in the books. He's strictly a New World deity. <br /> <br /> The good news is that the Scion Companion book should be coming out soon and it will have the Loa in it, including the good Baron.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">&quot;We have done the impossible, and that makes us mighty.&quot;<br /> Captain Malcolm Reynolds</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/679-unnatural1","name":"unnatural1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T03:46:46-07:00","id":1387229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387220-which-of-the-orisha-corresponds-to-baron-samedi#post1387220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the other guys in my RPG group is talking about running Scion. One idea I have for a character is a scion of Baron Samedi, the loa of the dead; but none of the Orisha list Baron Samedi as an alias. The books I have are Scion 2e Origin and Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>As said, as a purely New World deity you\u2019ll have to wait for the Companion for a writeup of the Baron in the \u201cLoa\u201d section.<br /> <br /> However, we have been informed that the Loa use the same Virtues and PSP (calling it a different name, but it works the same) as the Orisha. As such, it will be easy for you to play a Scion of the Baron without having to wait. You just needs your Calling (at Origin level) or one of your three Callings (at Hero level) to conceivably fit the Baron. And at Hero level you need a single Purview that comes from the Baron rather than from a Birthright. Death is the most obvious choice, but there are several others you can likely justify with your Storyguide if you\u2019d rather something else. I\u2019d be surprised if he didn\u2019t have Epic Stamina, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-10-2020, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T04:49:31-07:00","id":1387250,"title":"","content":"The Baron is definitely a Trickster. He is the Guardian of the cemetery. And if anyone is Liminal it's him. <br /> <br /> Death, Journeys (he represents the final one) are definitely Purviews. I'd add Deception as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-10T07:35:49-07:00","id":1387269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1387220-which-of-the-orisha-corresponds-to-baron-samedi?p=1387250#post1387250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Baron is definitely a Trickster. He is the Guardian of the cemetery. And if anyone is Liminal it's him.<br /> <br /> Death, Journeys (he represents the final one) are definitely Purviews. I'd add Deception as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting approach. Definitely agree on the Callings. The purviews, I would add Darkness and Deception (it would be mandatory), maybe also Artistry.<br /> <br /> in the 1E version he have Epic Charisma (that is more Deception than anything else in his case) and Earth, but I would put his powers more related to the graves than earth in general. The Artistry would come from the remaining part of Earth mixed with Epic Charisma. Don\u2019t know, the Baron is probably the most famous of the Loa, even people that don\u2019t know the loa still know his imagery. Makes sense to me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}